## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design secure, scalable multi-tenant inference with cross-account PrivateLink, model registry usage, and drift-aware rollouts under cost constraints.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Model Registry and Pipelines
- PrivateLink across AWS accounts
- Multi-tenant isolation strategies (shared vs. per-tenant containers)
- Drift detection with SageMaker Clarify
- Canary rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function routeTenant(input, modelRegistry) {
  const tenant = input.tenantId;
  if (!allowedTenants.has(tenant)) {
    throw new Error('Unauthorized tenant');
  }
  const modelVersion = modelRegistry.getModelVersion(tenant, 'latest');
  return invokeSageMaker(modelVersion.endpoint, input);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses design for multi-tenant ML services with strict data residency, private networking, and production-grade reliability, including canarying, drift handling, and cost accounting.

## Key Concepts

- PrivateLink and VPC isolation
- Multi-tenant routing architectures (per-tenant vs shared endpoint)
- Canary deployments with automatic rollback on drift/latency
- SageMaker Model Monitor for drift and quality checks
- KMS encryption and data residency controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-routing logic (illustrative only)
function routeRequest(tenantId, payload) {
  const endpoint = selectEndpointForTenant(tenantId);
  return invokeSageMaker(endpoint, payload);
}

function selectEndpointForTenant(tenantId) {
  // tenants mapped to endpoints or routing keys
  const map = {
    't1': 'endpoint-arn-1',
    't2': 'endpoint-arn-2'
  };
  return map[tenantId] || 'shared-endpoint-arn';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you design per-tenant quotas and rate limiting to prevent tail latency spikes?
- What metrics and alerting would you configure to detect drift early and trigger rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical use of SageMaker multi-model endpoints, per-tenant routing, and controlled releases under data privacy constraints (PrivateLink). It blends model choice, infrastructure sizing, and a measurable validation plan suitable for entry-level engineers.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker multi-model endpoints and Model Registry
- Tenant-aware routing with API Gateway + Lambda
- PrivateLink data isolation and VPC considerations
- Canary rollouts and rollback criteria

## Code Example
